51
00:56:04.000 --> 00:57:08.000
One witness reported seeing two women who matched Joanne and Caroline's description getting into a combivian with a male driver, which received strong media focus and generated hundreds of further tips. But police weren't convinced that it had been an accurate sighting. Further complicating efforts was the discovery that two young women with British accents were travelling a similar route to the one Joanne and Caroline planned to follow, meaning witness sightings could be confusing this separate set of travellers for the missing pair. Over the following two months, calls continued to come through and police followed up every lead, but none of the sightings were proven to be Joanne or Caroline. In August 1992, Joanne's parents Ray and Jill Walters travelled to Australia to assist the search for their missing daughter. They participated in press conferences, making an urgent appeal to the public for anyone with information to come forward.
一名目击者报告说看到两名外貌符合乔安妮和卡罗琳特征的女性上了一辆由男性司机驾驶的国民露营车，这受到了媒体的高度关注，并引发了数百条进一步的线索。但警方并不确信这是一个准确的目击情报。使调查进一步复杂化的是，人们发现有两名带有英国口音的年轻女性正沿着乔安妮和卡罗琳计划遵循的类似路线旅行，这意味着目击者的 sightings 可能会将这批不同的旅行者与失踪的两人混淆。在接下来的两个月里，电话源源不断地打进来，警方跟进了每一条线索，但没有一起目击事件被证明是乔安妮或卡罗琳。1992年8月，乔安妮的父母雷和吉尔·沃尔特斯前往澳大利亚协助搜寻他们失踪的女儿。他们参加了新闻发布会，向公众发出紧急呼吁，希望知情者提供线索。

52
00:57:08.000 --> 00:58:14.000
Ray Walters told the gathering media, Joanne didn't do anything on the spur of the moment. If she turned right or she turned left, she'd let us know. On the day Joanne and Caroline were last seen in Sydney, only four months had passed since Gabor, Nugabella and Daniel Habschede had disappeared from the same area, and their case was still gaining media attention as their devastated families travelled the country searching for clues. Given that both pairs of international backpackers had vanished from the King's Cross District, the press were quick to link the two disappearances. New South Wales police refused to confirm whether there was a connection, simply advising they were considering all possibilities. Joanne and Caroline's case continued to gain an increasing amount of media attention, leading the press to look into other recent incidents where international tourists had gone missing under similar circumstances.
雷·沃尔特斯对聚集的媒体说：“乔安妮从来不做冲动的事。如果她向右转或向左转，她会让我们知道的。”在乔安妮和卡罗琳最后一次在悉尼被看到的那天，距离加博尔、努加贝拉和丹尼尔·哈布舍德从同一地区失踪仅仅过去了四个月，随着他们心碎的家人在全国各地寻找线索，他们的案件仍在获得媒体关注。鉴于这两对国际背包客都在国王十字区失踪，媒体很快将这两起失踪案联系起来。新南威尔士州警方拒绝证实是否存在某种联系，只是表示他们正在考虑所有可能性。乔安妮和卡罗琳的案件继续获得越来越多的媒体关注，促使媒体调查其他国际游客在类似情况下失踪的近期事件。

53
00:58:14.000 --> 00:59:12.000
The mysterious disappearance of German backpacker Simone Schmidl two years earlier was mentioned from time to time, but very little was said about James Gibson and Deborah Everest, given they were Australian citizens travelling within their home country. Countless articles debating the safety risks involved with backpacking and hitchhiking were published, with the hostel industry coming under scrutiny. Hostel owners maintained Australia was a safe country and there was nothing for travellers to worry about, but the negative press was threatening to tarnish the thriving backpacker tourism industry. Despite this, young travellers were not deterred from hitchhiking. Many provided interviews to the media stating they had never encountered any issues while hitchhiking across the country, and had no intention of stopping, defending it as an affordable mode of transport.
德国背包客西蒙娜·施密德尔两年前神秘失踪的事件偶尔被提及，但关于詹姆斯·吉布森和黛博拉·埃弗里斯特的事情却很少被提及，因为他们是在国内旅行的澳大利亚公民。无数关于背包旅行和搭便车所涉安全风险的讨论文章发表，旅舍行业也受到了审查。旅舍业主坚持认为澳大利亚是一个安全的国家，旅行者无需担心，但负面新闻威胁到了蓬勃发展的背包客旅游业。尽管如此，年轻的旅行者并没有被搭便车吓退。许多人接受了媒体采访，称他们在全国搭便车时从未遇到过任何问题，并不打算停止，并为这是一种经济实惠的交通方式进行辩护。

54
00:59:12.000 --> 01:00:19.000
Police called for the establishment of a central registry to record the names and contact addresses for all foreigners travelling in Australia to help keep track of their movements. Although that may have been a useful tool, it was too late for the families of the seven backpackers who mysteriously vanished in Sydney between 1989. and 1992. On September 19, 1992, eight members of the Scrub Runners Orientering Club ventured down the Hume Highway, passing the kilometres of pine plantations before reaching the natural bush portion of Balangelo State Forest. From the rangers' huts, the team separated into pairs and ventured into the thick scrub as part of a training exercise. Two members, Keith Sealy and Keith Caldwell, partnered up and began navigating the steep rocky terrain west of the Longacre Fire Trail, heading towards an area known as Executioner's Drop.
警方呼吁建立一个中央登记处，记录所有在澳大利亚旅行的外国人的姓名和联系地址，以帮助追踪他们的行踪。尽管这可能是一个有用的工具，但对于自1989年至1992年在悉尼神秘失踪的七名背包客的家人来说，已经太晚了。1992年9月19日，斯劳布奔跑者定向越野俱乐部的八名成员沿着休姆高速公路冒险，穿过数公里的松树林，到达了巴兰杰洛州立森林的天然灌木林部分。从护林员的小屋出发，团队分成小组，作为训练练习的一部分，冒险进入了厚厚的灌木丛。两名成员基思·西利和基思·考德威尔结伴，开始在朗埃克火路以西陡峭的岩石地形中导航，向一个被称为“行刑点”的区域前进。

55
01:00:19.000 --> 01:01:09.000
At 4.15pm, the two men trekked into a shallow gully and made their way towards a large boulder. As they walked closer, they were hit with an overwhelming stench, which they assumed was emanating from a dead animal. They edged closer to the boulder, where they noticed a pile of sticks and branches on its western side, forming a mound approximately two metres long and 60 centimetres high. Out of the debris, they noticed a tuft of dark fur. They figured it must have been a dead wombat or a kangaroo. But upon closer inspection, they noticed a thin bone sticking out of the mound, along with a heel of a shoe and a patch of clothing.
下午4点15分，两名男子跋涉进入一条浅沟壑，朝一块大石头走去。随着他们走近，他们闻到了一股浓烈得令人窒息的恶臭，他们以为是从死动物身上散发出来的。他们向大石头靠得更近，注意到它西侧有一堆木棍和树枝，形成了一个大约两米长、60厘米高的小丘。在残骸中，他们注意到一撮黑色的毛皮。他们以为那一定是一只死袋娘或袋鼠。但在仔细检查后，他们注意到一根细骨头从土堆中伸出来，还有一只鞋子的后跟和一块衣物。

56
01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:49.000
Keith Sealy, quote, What I thought was the kangaroo leg was an elbow. The wombat was the hair on the back of a head. The men hastily made the two kilometre trek back to the closest rangers hut, where they contacted police and escorted them to the human remains. A crime scene was established as twilight descended, with floodlights illuminating the deserted area as police uncovered the heavily decomposed body of a young woman, facedown and gagged with strips torn from a shirt.
基思·西利引述道：“我以为是袋鼠腿的东西其实是手肘。袋鼠其实是脑后勺的头发。”两男子匆忙跋涉两公里回到最近的护林员小屋，他们联系了警方并护送他们前往人体遗骸所在地。随着黄昏降临，犯罪现场被建立起来，泛光灯照亮了荒凉的区域，警方在那里发掘出一名年轻女性严重腐烂的尸体，面朝下，嘴里塞着用衬衫撕下的布条。

57
01:01:49.000 --> 01:02:34.000
A search of the rugged terrain was put temporarily on hold due to the pitch darkness, with police commencing a thorough search of the site at daybreak. That next morning, just 30 metres from the skeletal remains discovered by the large boulder in the shallow gully, police noticed a similar mound of sticks and branches piled alongside a fallen log. Hidden underneath was a second body. When news of the gruesome discoveries in Belangelo State Forest hid the media, speculation ran rife as to whether more bodies would be uncovered at the site. In response, a police spokesperson said,
由于漆黑一片，对崎岖地形的搜查被暂时搁置，警方在天亮时对现场进行了彻底搜查。第二天早晨，距离浅沟壑大石头处发现的骸骨仅30米远，警方注意到一堆类似的木棍和树枝堆放在一根倒下的圆木旁。隐藏在下方的是第二具尸体。当巴兰杰洛州立森林恐怖发现的消息登上媒体时，关于该地点是否会发掘出更多尸体的猜测甚嚣尘上。作为回应，一名警方发言人说：

58
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:39.000
There is nothing to suggest that it's a mass grave, but we're keeping an open mind about what might be out there. To be continued next week. Thank you for watching. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
